From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Spatiand build <claude@prasetya.id>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:35:56 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Spatiand: the Mac builds what Cromite and Spatiand made
 for other systems

Cromite builds for Android, Windows and Linux, and Spatiand's patches for Linux; on a Mac five
places failed, each now as it is where it builds:
- SpatiKey's socket (patch 0010) is made with SOCK_CLOEXEC, which macOS has not got: closed on
  exec by fcntl instead.
- Cromite's "Add bookmark import/export actions" makes SelectFileDialog::ShowToast abstract and
  gives it to Android, Windows and Linux: the Mac's does nothing, as Linux's does.
- The unexportable-key flag and its debug page need bound session credentials, which Cromite
  turns off: both left out without them, as the feature itself is.
- On-device translation is off in Cromite: the Mac's sandbox no longer asks for its component.
- The profile menu's lock buttons (patch 0012) call Spatiand's profiles, which are Linux's only as
  yet (chrome/browser/spatiand): left out elsewhere, as every other Spatiand hook is. The proper
  way is that layer built on the Mac too.

Built on littleotter (2026-11-10): SpatiMesh.app links and loads a page headless.
---
 chrome/browser/about_flags.cc                              | 3 ++-
 chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc            | 3 +++
 chrome/browser/ui/views/profiles/profile_menu_view.cc      | 7 +++++++
 .../unexportable_keys_internals_ui.cc                      | 5 +++++
 components/spatikey/client.cc                              | 7 ++++++-
 ui/shell_dialogs/select_file_dialog_mac.h                  | 2 ++
 6 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

